./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0034/committee2/systems_reviewer.out:10:SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold on the provided evidence. The artifact is L0 CPU simulation, not real tau-bench/AppWorld/SWE-agent rollouts. Lead-time coverage is 42.4% >=1 step early, below the pre-registered >0.5 bar. At realistic strong stepwise-evaluator calibration from cited prior work, about 0.9 AUROC, the packet's own sweep says the monitor loses.
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0034/committee2/systems_reviewer.out:11:RATIONALE: prompt_version=v001. RED because the load-bearing systems claim is already occupied by online/stepwise failure detection prior art, and the claimed external monitor only beats naive verbalized confidence after confidence AUROC drops below about 0.72. It does not beat modeled self-confidence at sigma_conf=0.35, d=-0.006 CI [-0.011,-0.001], and published stepwise/critic baselines cited in the packet report about 0.9/0.94 AUROC. The robust +0.095 over static difficulty is insufficient as a systems insight because PRM/progress-rate systems already cover step/progress scoring, and the surviving lead-time framing failed its own L0 threshold.
